L1 Knowledge Base: Sign-in Is Slow or Not Working (Floor 6)
v 1.0, 07/08/2026, status : Draft

If your sign-in is very slow or does not complete, this guide explains what you can safely do.

First, reassurance
Your files and data are safe. This issue affects getting into your work computer, not your saved documents.

What you can do yourself
1. Wait for 2 to 3 minutes on the sign-in screen.
   Expected result: You are signed in and your desktop opens.

2. If nothing changes, restart your computer once.
   Expected result: Sign-in works after restart.

3. Sign in again and wait up to 3 minutes.
   Expected result: Your desktop opens normally.

4. If sign-in still fails or is very slow, stop trying repeated restarts.
   Expected result: You avoid making the delay worse and can get faster help.

5. Contact the Service Desk.
   Expected result: Support can check and fix the issue for you.

Details to include in your ticket
Please share these details when you contact the Service Desk:
- Your full name
- Your team and floor/location
- The computer name (if known)
- The exact time the issue happened
- What you saw (for example: stuck at sign-in, very slow sign-in)
- Whether a restart was tried
- Whether the second sign-in attempt worked
- A screenshot or photo of the screen, if possible

Important
Do not change settings, remove files, or try advanced fixes yourself.

Contact the service desk if...
Contact the Service Desk if sign-in takes more than 3 minutes, fails again after one restart, or you cannot reach your desktop.